t3oxide source adaptations

The primary Go terminal client uses the unmodified MIT-licensed Charm modules:
charm.land/bubbletea/v2 v2.1.0, charm.land/bubbles/v2 v2.2.1,
charm.land/lipgloss/v2 v2.0.6, and charm.land/glamour/v2 v2.0.1.
Their original license texts are in LICENSES/. Exact release/source provenance
is recorded in docs/dependencies.json; Go module checksums are in go.sum.
The interface uses those libraries directly. It does not depend on core-tui.
The transport and recovery code were reused from the separately delivered Go
core-tui alternative for this same project, then adapted into a T3-specific
session layer; that alternative's UI source is not bundled here.

adapter/core.mjs, adapter/t3.mjs, adapter/models.mjs, adapter/navigation.mjs
and adapter/native.mjs
adapt narrow command, response, catalog, lineage and event
structures from pingdotgg/t3code at 0e7346ccd9427c06161e222319e718e6bd70887f.
adapter/wire.mjs implements the narrow Effect RPC envelopes documented in that
repository's .repos/effect-smol RpcMessage.ts. These are adapted client-side
contracts, not a bundled copy of the full T3 runtime. See docs/architecture.md
and docs/model-navigation.md.

Native workflow extension 1 independently implements bounded project/default,
launch, inbox lifecycle and review presentation over those verified native
contracts. Its JSONC/default-file behavior follows the pinned public contract;
it bundles no Effect schema runtime or native execution service. See
docs/native-workflows.md for exact source references and compatibility limits.

